The carved instance icons that lived in `icons/` were removed with the shell that
drew them.

They were PNGs mapped out of the Prism Launcher binary (`prismlauncher.exe`),
(c) Prism Launcher contributors, GPL-3.0-only, kept under this workspace's own
GPL-3.0-only licence. Their reader was `crates/palantir-desktop/src/icons.rs`,
whose only caller was the old shell (`app.rs`); when that shell was deleted
nothing was left to draw them, so the art went with its reader instead of staying
in the tree as files nothing references.

The mapping, for `git log`'s benefit (carved filename -> meaning -> canonical
name) -- all that is left of them:

- 128x128_5178_169.png = chicken head -> chicken_legacy.png
- 50x50_1246_137.png = enderman head -> enderman_legacy.png
- 128x128_18345_174.png = enderpearl orb -> enderpearl_legacy.png
- 48x48_4526_119.png = grass block -> default.png and grass.png
  (byte-identical copies; Prism's default icon IS the grass block)
- 32x32_405_107.png = dirt -> dirt.png
- 32x32_757_103.png = steve head -> steve.png
- 32x32_1361_109.png = creeper -> creeper.png
- 32x32_228_108.png = TNT -> tnt.png
- 32x32_2270_93.png = yellow gear -> gear.png

What ships now: the launcher's own chrome is the reference Modrinth App's icon
set, compiled from its vendored SVGs by `tools/gen_icons.py` into `icons_gen.rs`
and stroked by `icon.rs` -- see `THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md`, which carries that
notice for the source and the binary -- plus the brand art in `assets/brand/`.
No Prism-derived art is shipped. Instance art, when an instance page draws it,
comes from the reference's own set on the same terms.
